/-
# Peterfalvi I Ch. I §6 Lemma 2 (pp. 159–160): coprime generation

Let `X` be a finite group of odd order, `u` an involution acting on `X` (so that `M = X⟨u⟩`),
and suppose `M` acts on a finite solvable group `Y` of order prime to `|M|`.  Then `Y` is
generated by the common fixed points of `J(X,u) = {x ∈ X | u x u⁻¹ = x⁻¹}` together with the
fixed points of the involutions of `M`.

Write `S = invSet X u` for the set of elements of `X` inverted by `u`, `A = ⟨S⟩ ≤ M`, and
`K = Ksub S Y = ⟨C_Y(A) ∪ ⋃_{v ∈ M, v² = 1} C_Y(v)⟩`.  The proof has three parts.

* `Ksub` is invariant under `M₀ = ⟨S,u⟩` (because `u` inverts every element of `S` and `S` is
  inversion closed, so `M₀` normalizes `⟨S⟩`; the union over the involutions is invariant under
  all of `M`).
* The `K = ⊥` lemma (`subsingleton_of_fix_eq_bot`): if the fixed points of `⟨S⟩` and of every
  involution of `M` are trivial, then so is `Y` — `u = 1 * u` is an involution, hence inverts
  `Y`, and so does every `x * u` (`x ∈ S`; it is an involution because `x * u ≠ 1`, as otherwise
  `u = x⁻¹ ∈ ⟨S⟩` would have order `2` dividing the odd number `|⟨S⟩|`), whence every `x ∈ S`
  acts trivially.
* `Ksub S Y = ⊤` follows by strong induction on `|Y|` (`Ksub_eq_top_aux`): if `Y` is commutative
  then `Ksub S Y` is normal and `M₀`-invariant and the `K = ⊥` lemma applied to the quotient by
  `Ksub S Y` (with the acting group `M₀`, using `C_{G/N}(A) = C_G(A)N/N` for coprime actions)
  gives `Y = Ksub S Y`; if `Y` is not commutative then `Y'` is a nontrivial proper `M`-invariant
  normal subgroup and the induction hypothesis for `↥Y'` and `Y ⧸ Y'` gives `Y' ≤ Ksub S Y` and
  `Ksub S Y ⊔ Y' = ⊤`, i.e. `Ksub S Y = ⊤`.

The main theorem `coprime_generation` follows by applying the master lemma to the acting group
`M₀ = ⟨S,u⟩` (the fixed points of `S` agree with those of `⟨S⟩`, and the involutions of `M₀` are
involutions of `M`).
-/
import Mathlib
import Submission.Work.ThreePoints.ThmC.Defs
import Submission.Work.Coprime.Basic
import Submission.Work.Coprime.fixedPoints_quotient
import Submission.Work.ThreePoints.ThmC.CoprimeGenDefs
import Submission.Work.ThreePoints.ThmC.map_Ksub_quotient

-- ftport:v435-opts-begin
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.instanceSearchTypes false
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false
